      "notes": "second seat on the same machine; the criteria were run, as stated here, and this is not an independent review: both seats are AI on one machine. Version 2 exists because version 1 could not pass: T1-c00 sets MEMEV_NO_SERVICE, which three Windows service tests inherited, and its body lost the end of its request to a cut at 4,000 characters. A rehearsal of version 2 through the real contractVerify, with a throwaway key on a clone that was its own vault, as a non-root user on a Linux server, then found four more faults, all now fixed or in this spec's scope: paths that only intermediate commits touched, a dated licence test that had begun to fail on every run, a commit bench that got no commit when its runner had a git identity, and a seeded bus folder that reads as uncommitted.  Read against version 1: no criterion statement or verifier changed; T6's one requirement now names first import as a guard, with the measured reason, 60.6 s against 200 s on that server, which narrows what T6-c03 shows and is stated in the results page; fourteen paths are added to the scope, under reviewer note 1. A limit that PR 451 adds, raised by the lead: where the vault is the workdir, a commit that adds code under a top-level bus/ escapes the scope check, as contracts/ already does; the memev repository tracks no bus/ folder. Timing tests can trip on a loaded machine: test/hooks-startup.test.mjs failed once under load, and T2-c03w failed once in 9 runs on a test not captured; a run that trips is rerun while nothing has landed on top, and the receipt names it. The second seat wrote PRs 446, 447, 449, 450 and 451, which this contract's range now holds, and the lead read them, so neither seat is independent of the other's work. Not done: power loss, a real vault at this size, Windows, or two computers through git.",
